1. MISSION AND DELIVERY STANDARD

You are working on Arvdoul — The Digital Nation, an ambitious, production-grade social platform.

Your assignment is to implement Part 1: Core Messaging Experience of Arvdoul's messaging ecosystem.

This is not a messaging prototype, visual demonstration, isolated chat component, or temporary MVP. It is the foundational direct-messaging system that future communication capabilities will extend.

The objective is to deliver a complete, reliable, secure, responsive, accessible, highly polished one-to-one messaging experience that can serve real users and scale with Arvdoul.

The implementation must feel like a carefully engineered native messaging product while remaining consistent with Arvdoul's existing architecture, brand identity, navigation, social graph, authentication, profile system, and Firebase infrastructure.

The quality target is an exceptional product combining the strongest usability characteristics of WhatsApp, Messenger, Snapchat, Instagram Direct and modern communication applications, while maintaining a distinctive Arvdoul identity.

Do not copy these products. Build a better, coherent Arvdoul messaging experience.

