5. CORE ARCHITECTURE

Build messaging as an integrated Arvdoul feature, not an isolated application within the application.

5.1 Architectural boundaries

Separate the messaging system into coherent layers.

Presentation layer

Responsible for screens, components, accessible interactions, UI state and visual behavior.

Application layer

Responsible for user actions and orchestration, including creating conversations, sending messages, uploading media, searching messages and managing requests.

Domain layer

Responsible for conversation rules, participant permissions, message types, delivery states, conversation policies and validation.

Data layer

Responsible for Firestore reads and writes, pagination, listeners, caching and persistence.

Infrastructure layer

Responsible for Firebase Auth, Firestore, Storage, Cloud Functions, FCM, network handling and observability.

Maintain the existing project conventions. These are architectural responsibilities, not a demand to introduce unnecessary abstraction layers.

