12. MESSAGE INTERACTIONS

All message actions must be contextually appropriate and genuinely operational.

12.1 Reply

Allow users to reply to a specific message.

Display:

- Original sender.
- Safe message preview.
- Appropriate media indicator.
- Navigation to the original message when available.

If the original message has been deleted, preserve a clear, non-misleading reply state.

Do not duplicate the entire original message inside every reply.

Use an authorized reference to the original message.

12.2 Reactions

Implement message reactions.

Requirements:

- Show available reactions.
- Add a reaction.
- Change a reaction.
- Remove a reaction.
- Show aggregate reaction counts.
- Show the current user's reaction.
- Update in real time.
- Prevent duplicate reactions from one user where the product policy permits only one reaction per user per message.

Use a data model that does not create excessive document reads.

Do not assume a user can react to a message they cannot access.

12.3 Forwarding

Allow a user to forward supported messages.

Requirements:

- Select an authorized target conversation.
- Preserve original content attribution where appropriate.
- Enforce access permissions.
- Preserve attachment access rules.
- Avoid copying unauthorized media.
- Prevent forwarding prohibited message types when applicable.
- Show appropriate forwarded context.

Forwarding must create a new authorized message action, not duplicate another user's entire database record or bypass their privacy settings.

12.4 Editing

Allow editing of eligible outgoing text messages.

Requirements:

- Only the original sender can edit.
- Enforce an explicit, documented edit policy.
- Validate edited content.
- Store edit metadata.
- Prevent unauthorized modification.
- Update the interface in real time.
- Display an edited indicator.
- Preserve consistency with message replies and search.

Do not allow an unrestricted client to edit arbitrary messages.

12.5 Deleting

Distinguish between:

Delete for me

- Hides the message from the current user's view using a user-specific state model.
- Does not unintentionally erase the recipient's copy.

Delete for everyone

- Must be authorized by the original sender.
- Must follow a documented server-enforced deletion policy.
- Must leave a safe tombstone or equivalent consistent state when required.
- Must not allow arbitrary deletion of another user's content.

Define these behaviors clearly.

Do not silently delete the shared conversation history when the user only intends to hide one message.

12.6 Additional actions

Include only actions that have real implementation and appropriate user value.

Contextual actions may include:

- Copy text.
- Select text.
- Reply.
- React.
- Forward.
- Edit.
- Delete.
- Report.

Do not overload the message action menu.

Respect touch targets, accessibility and platform interaction expectations.


