13. SHARING ARVDOUL CONTENT

Messaging must connect naturally to Arvdoul's content ecosystem.

This Part 1 integration covers existing supported content types only.

13.1 Supported content references

Integrate sharing for existing:

- Posts.
- Vibes.
- Sparks.

Before implementing an adapter, inspect each content system and discover its actual:

- Entity ID.
- Author ID.
- Content type.
- Visibility rules.
- Deletion behavior.
- Access policy.
- Canonical route or deep link.
- Media representation.
- Existing share service.

Do not invent new content identifiers or duplicate content records.

13.2 Share by reference

When sharing a Post, Vibe or Spark, create a message containing a validated content reference.

Do not copy the full original media and content into the message database.

The reference must point to the authoritative source.

A logical shared-content payload may contain:

interface SharedContentReference {
  contentType: "post" | "vibe" | "spark";
  contentId: string;
  authorId: string;
  createdAt?: Timestamp;
}

Adapt it to the actual content systems.

13.3 Permission-aware rendering

Before displaying shared content:

- Verify the current user's access.
- Resolve the authoritative content.
- Respect privacy settings.
- Respect blocking and restrictions.
- Handle removed content.
- Handle expired content.
- Handle unavailable content.
- Handle changed visibility.
- Handle deleted authors or unavailable profiles.

If content is unavailable, display an appropriate unavailable-content state.

Do not display private content merely because a user possesses its identifier.

13.4 Sharing flow

A user should be able to share supported content into an existing direct conversation through an intentional share experience.

The flow must:

1. Open a recipient selection experience.
2. Show eligible recipients.
3. Allow conversation selection.
4. Validate permissions.
5. Create the appropriate shared-content message.
6. Confirm the result accurately.
7. Provide a route to the shared conversation when appropriate.

Do not add recipient-selection screens that duplicate an existing Arvdoul share system.

Reuse existing infrastructure where possible.


