16. CONVERSATION SEARCH AND MESSAGE SEARCH

Search must be useful, accurate and secure.

16.1 Inbox search

Allow users to locate conversations by:

- Participant display name.
- Username.
- Supported profile identity fields.

Use the existing profile search or indexing service where appropriate.

Do not download every user's profile to perform client-side search.

16.2 Message search

Support searching messages in conversations the user is authorized to access.

Search behavior should include:

- Query validation.
- Pagination.
- Loading state.
- Empty state.
- Error state.
- Result previews.
- Conversation identification.
- Result timestamps.
- Safe navigation to the relevant message.

Preserve permission boundaries.

Do not leak messages from conversations that the user cannot access.

16.3 Search architecture

Inspect whether the application already has a search infrastructure capable of securely supporting messaging.

Firestore alone is not a full-text search engine.

Do not pretend that a limited substring query is equivalent to scalable full-text search.

If an existing search service is available, extend it.

If no suitable service exists, implement a clearly scoped, efficient Part 1 search strategy and document its limitations.

Do not add an expensive external search platform without justification.

16.4 Search indexing and deletion

Ensure edited and deleted messages do not leave misleading search results.

Indexing must not become an authorization bypass.

Respect retention and privacy rules.


