26. DATA MIGRATION AND BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY

Do not casually modify existing user or application schemas.

Before a migration:

1. Inspect the current schema.
2. Identify all existing readers and writers.
3. Identify all dependent Cloud Functions.
4. Identify relevant security rules.
5. Determine whether old clients may still access the database.
6. Define the migration sequence.
7. Make the migration idempotent.
8. Define rollback or compatibility behavior.
9. Test with existing and migrated records.
10. Document the expected operational impact.

If a new messaging schema is necessary, prefer additive and backward-compatible changes.

Do not delete existing collections merely to achieve a cleaner design.

Do not introduce a migration that requires every existing user to log in simultaneously.


